================================================================================
Third-party components redistributed in the published extension images
================================================================================

The container images built from this repository (ghcr.io/<org>/talos-coco-extension
and ghcr.io/<org>/talos-coco-nvidia) are Talos Linux system extensions. They do
not contain only this repository's source: they redistribute prebuilt binaries
and images taken from the upstream Kata Containers release tarball
(kata-static-<version>-amd64.tar.zst), published at:

    https://github.com/kata-containers/kata-containers/releases

Those components carry their own licenses, which are NOT Apache-2.0. The
Apache-2.0 license in LICENSE applies to this repository's own source only.

Components redistributed, and their licenses:

  QEMU (qemu-system-x86_64, qemu-system-x86_64-snp-experimental, and the
  associated firmware/ROM datadirs under share/kata-qemu/ and
  share/kata-qemu-snp-experimental/)
      GNU General Public License, version 2
      https://github.com/qemu/qemu  /  https://github.com/confidential-containers/qemu
      The SNP-experimental build originates from the Confidential Containers
      project's QEMU fork.

  Kata Containers (containerd-shim-kata-v2, guest kernel, guest images)
      Apache License 2.0
      https://github.com/kata-containers/kata-containers
      The shim is rebuilt from upstream source by this repository; the guest
      kernel (Linux, GPLv2) and guest images (Ubuntu-based rootfs, containing
      many separately licensed components) are redistributed as built upstream.

  virtiofsd
      Apache License 2.0 / BSD-3-Clause
      https://gitlab.com/virtio-fs/virtiofsd

  EDK2 / OVMF (share/ovmf/AMDSEV.fd)
      BSD-2-Clause-Patent
      https://github.com/tianocore/edk2

  BusyBox (extension-service runtime in the NVIDIA add-on)
      GNU General Public License, version 2
      https://busybox.net

  NVIDIA GPU driver and NVRC (inside the NVIDIA confidential guest image)
      NVIDIA proprietary license terms; the open GPU kernel modules are
      dual-licensed MIT/GPLv2.
      https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/drivers/  /  https://github.com/NVIDIA/open-gpu-kernel-modules

================================================================================
Source availability
================================================================================

The GPLv2 components above are redistributed unmodified from their upstream
release artifacts. Corresponding source is available from the upstream projects
at the URLs listed, at the exact versions pinned in this repository. Most are
taken from the kata-static release tarball, fixed by KATA_VERSION (+ its
sha256) in the Makefile and both Dockerfiles; BusyBox is pinned separately via
`FROM busybox:1.36.1-musl` in extensions/coco-nvidia/Dockerfile.
